  "body": "stacked on #955 - this diff shows #955's commits until it merges; merge #955 first.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n- G-code window code is selectable: drag across lines, Ctrl+C copies the G-code. The line numbers are now a separate non-selectable label, so a copy never carries them.\r\n- The cursor row (the line that drives the amber segment in the viewport) has a background band in the theme's selection colour. Syntax colours still show on it.\r\n- Clicking a row anywhere moves the cursor to it (the scroll centres the row; the cursor law reads it back). Ephemeral view state only, no command.\r\n- Ticking the trace box no longer makes the window grow over the part: egui's `Sides` fed the listing an unbounded width in the auto-sized window (the new test measured 5144 px wide); the trace view now lays its two panes into fixed rects cut from the window's own free rect.\r\n- The viewer moved from `pages.rs` (1927 lines) to `gcode_view.rs`; coloured text unchanged (`gcode_highlight.rs` gained `gutter_text`).\r\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/1089-gcode-window.md`.\r\n\r\n## Not changed\r\n- Trace default: `PostView::trace` is created `false`. What the reporter saw as \"tracing on\" is the amber viewport segment for the listing's cursor, always shown while the viewer is open (M1.7d). Intended.\r\n- No right-click Copy menu (Ctrl+C only); no snapshot PNG touched.\r\n- Nothing owed on clicks: a click on ANY row, first and last half page included, puts the cursor (band and amber segment) on exactly that row. The cursor is a pin (clicked row, settled middle row) in egui temp memory, released by any scroll that moves the middle row; see the decision file.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib gcode` (13 pass), `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green. Pinning tests in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/gcode_viewer.rs`: `ticking_trace_keeps_the_window_its_size`, `clicking_a_line_moves_the_cursor_there` (first row, top half page, middle, last row), `the_cursor_line_is_highlighted`, `dragging_across_lines_and_copying_takes_the_code_not_the_numbers`.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\nNot seen on screen (no GUI launched); the width, highlight and copy are checked headlessly through egui_kittest only. Real clipboard and right-click menu untested.\r\n\r\nChangelog: G-code window: selectable and copyable code, highlighted cursor line, click a line to move the trace, and the trace box no longer widens the window (#1089, PR #1090)\r\nEffort: medium\r\n\r\nFixes #1089\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
